  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate adaptation, mitigation, environment and biodiversity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In May 2023, Australia provided funding for phase one of the Tuvalu Coastal Adaptation Project (TCAP). The project supported Tuvalu to develop a long-term coastal adaptation strategy and build capacity of local communities, and national and local authorities, to better implement the adaptation strategy. A sustainable financing mechanism was established to support these long-term adaptation efforts. TCAP also supported implementation of protection measures to reduce vulnerability of key coastal infrastructure including homes, schools and medical centres across three islands (Funafuti, Nanumaga and Nanumea). These measures also helped address issues of overcrowding and limited space for key infrastructure, creating safe land that is critical to protect the lives, livelihoods and culture of Tuvaluans in the face of climate change. The data collected for this project (including topographic mapping and wave modelling) has filled gaps in understanding of the environment and will inform adaptation efforts into future decades.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the Australian Pacific Partnerships Platform, Australia supported expert advice to Tuvalu&#x2019;s Ministry of Finance and Treasury. The Public Financial Management adviser assisted with policy and planning, budget development and management, financial reporting and continued development and implementation of Tuvalu&#x2019;s financial management information system (FMIS). They also provided strategic advice on managing public funds. This support enabled improvements in local staff uptake and ownership of the FMIS. Staff also displayed greater awareness of financial management and expenditure control, as well as the importance of budget execution.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the Australian Pacific Partnerships Platform, a Performance Audit Adviser (PAA) supported Tuvalu&#x2019;s Office of the Auditor General (TOAG) to conduct performance audits and contribute to prudent management of public resources and macroeconomic resilience in Tuvalu. The PAA developed a performance audit manual, quality assured by the Pacific Association of Supreme Audit Institutions. TOAG staff are using the manual to guide performance audits, contributing to the sustainability of this initiative. The PAA supported TOAG to conduct a performance audit of the Tuvalu Overseas Medical Referral Scheme. The audit report will help strengthen the Scheme&#x2019;s effectiveness and efficiency.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
